  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project on Supporting Human Rights defenders and strengthening Civil Society in promoting and protecting democracy in UVA Province</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project has three main aims. Providing opportunity for grassroots level HRDs to develop concrete ways to hold public and private officials and institutions accountable for human rights violations, Supporting and  strengthening of civil society to safeguard human rights and address human rights violations in a peaceful manner whilst protecting democracy and fundamental freedoms of the people are two of them. Project also aims to provide practical support to community level field workers to achieves the objectives of their CSOs in safeguarding and protecting human rights violations. The project propose multipronged approach to achieve above aims though the project. The project organizes, facilitates, and supports capacity development and training intervention for decision-makers and stakeholders of civil society organizations on human rights protection and prevention of abuses. The project also targets at promoting gender equality and social inclusion, including youth empowerment. It will also strengthen the competence and capacity of HRDs to effectively carry out their role in strengthening civil society space for protecting human rights, through monitoring, investigation, reporting and complaints handling functions. The project will be implemented with the support and coordination of District Consortia in Monaragala and Badulla Districts in the UVA Province. (District Consortia is an umbrella organization which has 35 community based organizations in Monaragala and in Badulla)</narrative>
  </description>
